Bengaluru Traffic Advisory: Diversions, Parking Restrictions Announced Around Halasuru Lake For Ganesh Idol Immersions From August 27 To 31
Bengaluru Traffic Advisory: Bengaluru Traffic Police has announced diversions from August 27–31 for Ganesh idol immersions at Halasuru Lake, where over 30,000 idols are expected. Restrictions will be enforced daily between 2 PM–4 AM. Alternative routes have been provided, and parking is banned near the lake. Citizens are urged to cooperate.
Bengaluru Traffic Advisory: Diversions Announced for Ganesh Idol Immersion at Halasuru Lake (Image/ Canva)
By
Deeksha Gour
Tue, 26 Aug 2025 06:11 PM (IST)
Source:
JND
Add as a preferred
Related Articles
Bengaluru Traffic Advisory:
Bengaluru City Traffic Police has issued a traffic advisory ahead of Ganesh idol immersions at Halasuru Lake Kalyani. The arrangements will be in place from August 27 to 31, when more than 30,000 idols are expected to be immersed. To handle the heavy rush, restrictions and diversions will be enforced every day between 2:00 PM and 4:00 AM.
Bengaluru Traffic Restriction For Ganeshotsav
Kensington Road will become one-way between the Kensington-Murphy Road Junction and MEG–Halasuru Lake stretch. Movement will be allowed only from MEG towards Kensington-Murphy Road. Similarly, traffic flow on Annaswamy Modaliyar Road will be altered in the direction leading to Halasuru Lake.
